# ⚠️ `client` stood here, from when that name meant the BUILT web interface
# (`yarn build --outDir ../client`). Since the repositories were merged it is
# the client's SOURCE tree — and the rule silently swallowed every new file
# added under it. Tracked files are unaffected by .gitignore, so the import
# itself looked fine; the first new test written afterwards simply never
# reached a commit, with no error anywhere. The build output is `dist-client/`
# now (see .github/workflows/build.yml) and that is what gets ignored.
dist-client
.gitignore

